WEBVTT

00:14.210 --> 00:15.410
This is...

00:18.310 --> 00:19.490
Garf!

00:23.050 --> 00:23.910
Those two...

00:24.690 --> 00:26.220
are real strong.

00:28.900 --> 00:30.050
Sounds fun.

00:30.050 --> 00:30.920
No!

00:31.620 --> 00:33.330
Don't, Garf!

00:33.330 --> 00:35.600
You and I can't handle them alone!

00:35.600 --> 00:37.430
But even if we try to turn tail and run,

00:37.910 --> 00:39.830
they aren't gonna let us.

00:39.830 --> 00:40.990
We gotta fight!

00:40.990 --> 00:42.680
A-All right, just once...

00:43.630 --> 00:46.180
We crash into them once, then dodge and run!

00:46.180 --> 00:47.150
It's the only way!

00:47.980 --> 00:49.360
Why are you here?!

00:53.690 --> 00:54.860
Fine.

00:55.340 --> 00:58.510
I'll rush 'em once and then bail for now.

00:58.510 --> 01:00.000
That's good enough, right?

01:00.000 --> 01:02.500
Yes! That's right! Let's do that!

01:03.280 --> 01:04.330
Here I come!

01:14.280 --> 01:17.640
Vice Captain, what is the meaning of this?

01:18.010 --> 01:20.320
Ain't that obvious?

01:20.320 --> 01:22.850
You stay right there. Don't move.

01:22.850 --> 01:25.940
You know what a hassle the Witch's Cult is.

01:26.470 --> 01:30.670
Gonna abandon your beloved 
master and your blood father

01:30.670 --> 01:34.350
to run off and help some 
people you don't even know?

01:34.350 --> 01:37.280
Hey, loser. What're you doing?

01:37.650 --> 01:40.010
That's all just talk to scare you.

01:40.010 --> 01:41.730
No need to worry.

01:41.730 --> 01:43.800
Wanna try me?

01:43.800 --> 01:45.960
It's not difficult.

01:46.240 --> 01:49.900
I'm just telling you to 
do your duty as a knight.

01:49.900 --> 01:53.440
You wanna talk about the succession 
of the Astrea family, right?

01:53.440 --> 01:54.620
Go, I said!

01:55.210 --> 01:55.880
Go!

01:57.150 --> 01:58.590
Felt-sama...

01:59.940 --> 02:00.900
I...

02:03.330 --> 02:04.770
The witch's remains?

02:05.570 --> 02:07.900
But the Witch of Envy isn't dead.

02:08.480 --> 02:08.980
I mean...

02:09.770 --> 02:12.780
You must come... to kill me.

02:14.770 --> 02:15.360
I mean—

02:15.360 --> 02:17.570
Relax, brother.

02:17.870 --> 02:20.090
Just because they say "the witch's remains"

02:20.090 --> 02:23.770
doesn't mean they're specifically 
talking about the Witch of Envy.

02:23.770 --> 02:27.350
That's right. There's not much 
talk of it in the records,

02:27.350 --> 02:29.710
but that kinda word-of-mouth 
story isn't uncommon.

02:30.220 --> 02:32.210
And in this city...

02:32.720 --> 02:36.170
There are remains belonging to 
one other than the Witch of Envy?

02:37.200 --> 02:39.490
Do you know where they are?

02:39.490 --> 02:40.530
No.

02:41.200 --> 02:44.890
The witch's remains are a crucial 
secret of the Watergate City.

02:44.890 --> 02:48.000
If anyone knows about 'em, 
it'd be the Council of Ten.

02:48.000 --> 02:51.020
The Council of Ten... So, Kiritaka?

02:53.950 --> 02:59.360
So what's the deal with this Capella 
Emerada Lugunica who's demanding them?

03:00.100 --> 03:04.640
Shouldn't only members of the royal 
family have the name "Lugunica"?

03:04.640 --> 03:06.600
She probably meant it as a taunt.

03:06.600 --> 03:09.960
Everyone's heard the story of how 
all the royals died of illness.

03:10.270 --> 03:13.170
I am uncertain about the 
origins of Capella's name,

03:13.170 --> 03:19.260
but there was once a member of the 
royal family called Emerada Lugunica.

03:19.680 --> 03:23.450
She lived over fifty years ago.

03:23.980 --> 03:27.260
It is said that she was a very 
beautiful, intelligent woman,

03:27.260 --> 03:30.230
but also as ruthless as one could be.

03:30.230 --> 03:32.600
All of the people feared her.

03:32.600 --> 03:35.450
Wait, wait! The mirror's reacting!

03:36.470 --> 03:37.440
Julius?

03:40.790 --> 03:42.880
It appears everyone is present.

03:42.880 --> 03:44.320
Can you all see me?

03:44.720 --> 03:47.210
I was worried when you didn't get in touch!

03:47.210 --> 03:49.040
How are things lookin' outside?

03:49.040 --> 03:49.840
Well...

03:49.840 --> 03:51.540
M-Milady!

03:51.540 --> 03:52.880
There's trouble!

03:52.880 --> 03:55.000
Has our sister made it back there yet?!

03:55.370 --> 03:59.160
No, she hasn't. We're worried, too.

03:59.160 --> 04:01.080
Milady! Milady, are you there?!

04:01.080 --> 04:01.970
It's Hetaro!

04:02.600 --> 04:05.940
Sis... Sis, she's...

04:05.940 --> 04:09.010
Hetaro, calm down. What happened?

04:09.010 --> 04:10.370
Take it slow.

04:10.370 --> 04:14.480
Th-The effects of our divine protection 
flowed from her into us...

04:14.480 --> 04:16.900
I-It was such a bad wound...

04:16.900 --> 04:20.100
Divine protection? You mean your Trisection?

04:20.100 --> 04:22.880
So wherever Mimi is, she's hurt—

04:21.410 --> 04:24.820
<i>Hey there! Hey there! Hey, hey, hey there!</i>

04:25.130 --> 04:29.580
<i>Are all you meat scraps doing good?</i>

04:29.850 --> 04:35.000
<i>Are you all aflutter at the 
beautiful sound of my voice?</i>

04:35.990 --> 04:38.370
<i>The truth is...</i>

04:38.370 --> 04:43.310
<i>Some bad people have attacked 
the city government office,</i>

04:39.590 --> 04:40.710
<i>Who's there?!</i>

04:43.310 --> 04:46.270
and I'm just utterly heartbroken!

04:45.010 --> 04:45.880
Sorry...

04:46.270 --> 04:48.780
S-Sorry, boss...

04:46.270 --> 04:50.410
<i>Really, you ignorant meat scraps 
disappointed me so much,</i>

04:50.410 --> 04:52.640
I'm... I'm...

04:50.410 --> 04:54.600
<i>I'm just completely dumbfounded!</i>

04:53.080 --> 04:54.600
I'm just a useless...

04:53.590 --> 04:54.600
Garfiel?

04:54.600 --> 04:56.810
...good-for-nothing!

05:05.770 --> 05:08.990
Why? The wound isn't closing!

05:08.990 --> 05:10.270
I need bandages!

05:18.890 --> 05:24.880
<i>I hope you raiders are realizing 
by now that it's done you no good!</i>

05:29.550 --> 05:31.800
<i>As representatives of those raiders,</i>

05:31.800 --> 05:34.920
<i>I'll start by slicing the ones 
who are still in this building</i>

05:34.920 --> 05:38.330
<i>into even tinier meat scraps!</i>

05:42.170 --> 05:43.390
What the hell...

05:43.990 --> 05:48.280
<i>If you don't like that, 
I have but one demand!</i>

05:48.280 --> 05:49.960
<i>The witch's remains!</i>

05:49.960 --> 05:52.180
<i>That's it! All done!</i>

05:52.180 --> 05:57.600
<i>Oh, my people and I have taken up positions 
in each of the watergate control towers,</i>

05:57.600 --> 06:00.310
<i>so you'd better not try anything funny!</i>

06:04.910 --> 06:07.230
Does she think this is a game?

06:08.720 --> 06:10.500
Are you all safe?

06:10.500 --> 06:11.140
Kiritaka!

06:11.510 --> 06:12.600
You're alive?!

06:13.460 --> 06:14.350
Barely.

06:14.650 --> 06:17.460
Otto isn't with you?

06:17.460 --> 06:19.760
I'm sorry, but no.

06:19.760 --> 06:20.560
I see...

06:21.200 --> 06:23.770
Knowing him, that's not 
too unexpected, but...

06:27.680 --> 06:30.070
Everyone, what you've heard is true.

06:30.800 --> 06:34.290
We haven't a moment to spare 
in saving the hostages.

06:34.290 --> 06:36.620
I'll get right to the point.

06:36.620 --> 06:39.400
These witch's remains 
really exist, don't they?

06:39.400 --> 06:40.830
Yes, they do.

06:41.480 --> 06:44.460
But there is no way to move them.

06:45.000 --> 06:48.660
Therefore, we cannot give 
her what she is demanding.

06:48.660 --> 06:52.680
When you say they can't be moved, 
is that merely your opinion?

06:53.240 --> 06:55.010
No, I meant it literally.

06:55.600 --> 06:57.980
It is physically impossible to move them.

06:59.360 --> 07:03.060
The witch's remains house a special power.

07:03.060 --> 07:04.460
If we move them,

07:04.460 --> 07:07.990
the damage would rival that of the time when 
the city was flooded to kill the witch—

07:07.990 --> 07:11.340
no, it would be even worse.

07:13.840 --> 07:16.160
It would destroy the city.

07:16.160 --> 07:20.470
Like what happened when 
Typhon was drowned, eh?

07:20.470 --> 07:22.680
We can't give her the remains.

07:22.680 --> 07:24.460
And we won't heed her stupid demands.

07:24.770 --> 07:26.360
That's not gonna change.

07:26.360 --> 07:28.090
Sis!

07:28.870 --> 07:31.930
Sis! Sis!

07:41.390 --> 07:43.020
I hadn't thanked you yet.

07:43.840 --> 07:46.810
If you hadn't brought her back here,

07:46.810 --> 07:48.860
there's no doubt Mimi would've died.

07:50.010 --> 07:51.820
So... we owe you.

07:52.460 --> 07:55.030
Thank you. Thank you so much.

07:55.760 --> 07:58.290
Stop it! I just...

07:58.290 --> 07:59.750
Garfiel.

08:00.390 --> 08:01.870
Tell me what happened.

08:01.870 --> 08:06.710
I have to take out all of the idiots 
who are attacking this city.

08:07.100 --> 08:10.200
To do that, I need your strength.

08:10.200 --> 08:12.470
I can't let you keep moping around forever.

08:17.760 --> 08:19.810
We heard... the broadcast.

08:20.650 --> 08:24.520
So the shrimp and I headed 
for the government office.

08:34.600 --> 08:35.360
You're mi—

08:42.870 --> 08:47.430
I'll love you only after I 
kill you, Garfiel Tinsel.

08:54.700 --> 08:55.380
What?!

09:04.260 --> 09:05.890
Heave-ho!

09:20.250 --> 09:21.120
Shrimp?

09:32.450 --> 09:34.260
A huge man with extra arms...

09:35.200 --> 09:36.090
and a woman?

09:36.780 --> 09:38.120
Wilhelm-san?

09:41.680 --> 09:44.060
This wound that will not close

09:44.500 --> 09:47.770
was probably the work of the divine 
protection of the Death God.

09:48.290 --> 09:52.100
The shrimp... She was tryin' to protect me...

09:52.100 --> 09:54.150
That was Mimi's choice.

09:54.550 --> 09:57.040
I know! I know that!

09:57.700 --> 10:01.520
No one... No one's gonna blame me.

10:01.520 --> 10:04.820
But that ain't the same for me!

10:04.820 --> 10:05.700
Oh?

10:06.080 --> 10:10.290
So I'm gonna kick that bastard's ass!

10:10.880 --> 10:12.660
A fine howl!

10:13.140 --> 10:14.760
A man never goes back on his word.

10:16.470 --> 10:18.930
So you're gonna get up and fight, yeah?

10:20.760 --> 10:23.120
Yeah! Damn right!

10:23.120 --> 10:25.970
I'm gonna get 'em!

10:27.050 --> 10:28.520
So, Subaru...

10:29.660 --> 10:31.980
What would you do next?

10:31.980 --> 10:35.900
You're being pretty damn vague again.

10:36.310 --> 10:38.880
I recalled the battle with Sloth.

10:38.880 --> 10:41.620
Perhaps you will be the 
"wonder drug." Remember that?

10:42.880 --> 10:44.700
Don't ask the impossible of me!

10:44.700 --> 10:46.700
If I was the Witch's Cult's wonder drug,

10:46.700 --> 10:49.260
my leg wouldn't look like this!

10:50.400 --> 10:53.040
It was Greed who took Emilia away.

10:53.460 --> 10:57.640
I don't want to leave her in his filthy 
hands one second longer than I have to.

10:57.640 --> 11:03.050
By which you mean your priority 
is getting Emilia-sama back?

11:05.190 --> 11:06.530
Of course it is.

11:09.890 --> 11:12.740
Or so I'd like to say, but...

11:12.740 --> 11:14.730
That metia is a problem.

11:15.960 --> 11:16.940
I agree.

11:17.730 --> 11:22.940
The voice that eats away at the 
minds of all who hear it, the metia,

11:22.940 --> 11:26.330
is serving as the chain that 
binds everyone in this city.

11:27.690 --> 11:32.120
Our first priority has to be the 
government office, where Lust is.

11:33.600 --> 11:37.840
Seein' you walk normally like this, 
it looks like you're doin' fine.

11:37.840 --> 11:41.070
I mean, strictly speaking, 
I'm not fine at all...

11:41.680 --> 11:45.080
But Felis has to treat the townspeople,

11:45.080 --> 11:46.680
and Hetaro and Tivey can't act since they're

11:46.680 --> 11:48.890
sharing Mimi's wound
through their divine protection.

11:49.500 --> 11:52.300
We need all the people we can get.

11:52.760 --> 11:53.850
Speaking of...

11:54.660 --> 11:57.460
Sorry to ask after you brought us this far,

11:57.460 --> 11:59.190
but can you fight, Crusch-san?

11:59.850 --> 12:02.320
I have retrained under Wilhelm.

12:03.230 --> 12:05.930
I will not hold you back, at the very least.

12:05.930 --> 12:08.660
Crusch-sama's natural talents 
have not diminished.

12:09.730 --> 12:11.370
I can guarantee that.

12:13.240 --> 12:14.760
And what about you?

12:15.920 --> 12:18.310
I've never actually seen you fight.

12:18.310 --> 12:21.380
Oh... Well, the thing about that, brother...

12:21.380 --> 12:24.480
It's gonna take some guts to 
say this right now, but...

12:24.480 --> 12:25.090
What?

12:26.030 --> 12:29.890
Sorry, but I gotta join another 
party to look for the princess.

12:29.890 --> 12:31.370
This is where we part ways.

12:31.370 --> 12:34.040
Huh?! What the hell are you saying?!

12:34.040 --> 12:36.720
C'mon, I said I was sorry.

12:36.720 --> 12:39.190
I apologize to the rest of you, too.

12:39.650 --> 12:43.600
It's only natural for a servant 
to put his master first.

12:43.600 --> 12:45.770
I wouldn't criticize you for that.

12:45.770 --> 12:47.240
Appreciate it.

12:48.310 --> 12:49.820
Are you serious?

12:49.820 --> 12:53.240
So now I'm the one who's 
guaranteed to hold us back, huh?

12:53.240 --> 12:56.710
Why say that? With you here, 
we've got the power of a hundred!

12:56.710 --> 12:57.840
We're countin' on you!

12:57.840 --> 12:58.380
Huh?

12:59.120 --> 13:01.490
Against both the White Whale and Sloth,

13:01.490 --> 13:04.010
we all saw how hard you went.

13:04.630 --> 13:06.980
I feel reassured, as well.

13:06.980 --> 13:09.100
I'm depending on you, Subaru-sama.

13:09.100 --> 13:11.360
R-Really?

13:11.360 --> 13:14.010
Well, now I feel kinda weird...

13:14.010 --> 13:16.520
Let me give you one piece of advice, then.

13:17.020 --> 13:20.360
If you come up against Gluttony, 
don't tell him your real name.

13:21.570 --> 13:26.180
It's possible that all of the Sin 
Archbishops are in this city right now.

13:26.180 --> 13:27.030
What?!

13:30.020 --> 13:33.370
If we're both lucky,
we'll meet again, brother.

13:43.120 --> 13:44.510
I smell blood.

13:45.360 --> 13:47.340
A whole lot of it.

13:48.490 --> 13:49.360
Subaru.

13:50.040 --> 13:51.340
You're getting too worked up.

13:52.740 --> 13:53.930
Sorry.

13:54.450 --> 13:55.930
You're right. I'm too worked up.

13:56.580 --> 13:59.980
I don't blame you. You have 
a history with Gluttony.

14:00.650 --> 14:03.230
If I were in your position,

14:03.230 --> 14:05.650
I'm not certain I could retain my composure.

14:05.650 --> 14:08.940
Man, what's with you? You're being creepy.

14:17.360 --> 14:19.440
We'll do this just as we discussed.

14:19.440 --> 14:21.380
In general, we'll take 
out each one in groups.

14:21.880 --> 14:25.280
We'll deal with each one individually 
and take back the government office.

14:25.280 --> 14:26.050
But...

14:26.530 --> 14:31.720
If we feel we're at a disadvantage,
 make the call to retreat at once. Right?

14:38.410 --> 14:41.270
The square's covered in the bodies of guards.

14:41.270 --> 14:43.340
Don't let that scare you outta this!

14:44.030 --> 14:44.860
Let's move!

14:48.530 --> 14:51.780
Hey, bro... 'scuse me a minute!

14:51.780 --> 14:54.080
Let's go!

14:51.780 --> 14:54.900
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

15:06.880 --> 15:08.060
What is...

15:10.340 --> 15:11.480
It's them!

15:13.740 --> 15:14.680
Let's go!

15:37.690 --> 15:38.830
So it's true...

15:45.540 --> 15:48.590
Four arms ain't nothin'!

15:50.300 --> 15:51.970
You're mine!

15:55.060 --> 15:56.300
Gotcha.

16:02.240 --> 16:03.100
Now!

16:07.830 --> 16:09.570
What the hell?!

16:09.570 --> 16:11.180
I don't think so!

16:13.130 --> 16:14.240
Composite Magic:

16:14.860 --> 16:16.160
Ul Gora!

16:22.460 --> 16:25.460
We hit them with everything 
we had and got nowhere?

16:26.050 --> 16:28.170
I'm pretty shocked right now.

16:28.560 --> 16:30.700
Okay, guys, one more time!

16:30.700 --> 16:33.940
Julius and Crusch-san's ranged 
attacks will be our main—

16:35.300 --> 16:38.640
<i>Oh, look at that! You really showed up!</i>

16:41.020 --> 16:44.910
<i>Well, then, let me introduce myself again!</i>

16:44.910 --> 16:49.250
<i>I'm the Sin Archbishop in the 
Witch's Cult representing lust,</i>

16:49.250 --> 16:53.130
<i>Capella Emerada Lugunica-chan-sama!</i>

16:54.120 --> 16:57.450
<i>Die! You rotten meat scraps!</i>

16:57.450 --> 16:59.250
Seriously?

16:59.250 --> 17:02.080
That's one chillingly expressive dragon.

17:02.080 --> 17:03.700
What's this?

17:03.700 --> 17:08.310
You there. So you're not an underdog,
but an undercat?

17:08.310 --> 17:09.960
Mew, mew, mew, mew!

17:09.960 --> 17:14.000
Are you crying because your 
little kitty mate is dead?

17:16.360 --> 17:17.480
Boss...

17:18.090 --> 17:19.910
Oh, shut up.

17:19.910 --> 17:24.020
Every time you speak, you're ruining
what dragon's are like in my head.

17:24.560 --> 17:25.570
<i>Huh?</i>

17:26.050 --> 17:27.600
<i>And just who are you?</i>

17:27.600 --> 17:32.070
<i>You smell particularly out of place 
among all the meat scraps here.</i>

17:32.070 --> 17:35.290
First of all, the way you 
do things is way too sloppy!

17:35.290 --> 17:38.480
You top brass should be showing up one at 
a time like the big shots you think you are!

17:38.480 --> 17:41.340
You clearly have no concept 
of beauty of form!

17:41.340 --> 17:45.000
Who do you think you are?! Some wannabe god?!

17:45.840 --> 17:48.110
There. All done buying us time.

17:48.110 --> 17:49.460
Get 'em, Julius!

17:50.620 --> 17:52.420
From the bottom of my heart,

17:53.190 --> 17:56.010
your recklessness truly shocks me sometimes.

17:56.490 --> 17:59.090
Burn in a flash of rainbow light!

17:59.480 --> 18:02.350
Al Clauseria!

18:02.350 --> 18:04.560
<i>You dare use such petty tricks against me?!</i>

18:10.110 --> 18:12.010
<i>Oh, goodness me.</i>

18:12.010 --> 18:17.920
<i>You shouldn't stare at someone from 
such an angle and get so excited.</i>

18:22.350 --> 18:24.740
Her wounds... are healing?

18:24.740 --> 18:26.530
You've gotta be kidding me!

18:26.530 --> 18:28.260
<i>Oopsie, oopsie...</i>

18:33.980 --> 18:37.170
<i>Aw, would you look at that?
The time has come.</i>

18:37.170 --> 18:40.010
<i>I'll be going back inside now.</i>

18:40.350 --> 18:42.100
Huh?! Hold up!

18:42.470 --> 18:48.330
<i>Look forward to seeing just how 
the little bugs in this cage suffer!</i>

18:52.550 --> 18:54.470
Does she intend to execute the hostages?

18:54.470 --> 18:58.700
Damn it! So we have no choice 
but to go inside now?

18:58.700 --> 19:01.050
We ain't got time to dawdle!

19:01.050 --> 19:03.530
We'll take care of those two!

19:05.560 --> 19:07.780
Garfiel! Don't you dare lose!

19:07.780 --> 19:10.080
Yep! Go get 'em, boss!

19:10.400 --> 19:12.580
Wilhelm, I leave this to you.

19:13.060 --> 19:14.420
Understood.

19:16.270 --> 19:16.880
Subaru!

19:17.360 --> 19:18.800
Take care of Crusch-sama!

19:18.800 --> 19:20.050
Whoa, wai—

19:21.840 --> 19:23.290
You damn...

19:23.290 --> 19:25.560
Sorry about this, Crusch-san!

19:30.190 --> 19:31.740
Hold on tight!

19:31.740 --> 19:32.520
Right!

19:42.610 --> 19:45.940
C-Crusch-san, you good?

19:45.940 --> 19:50.420
I-I'm all right... but 
Subaru-sama, your leg...

19:50.420 --> 19:53.540
I-I'm just fine. Doesn't hurt a bit.

20:01.720 --> 20:06.130
Hey, calm down, my dudes and my lady.

20:06.130 --> 20:08.770
I'm so happy. So happy.

20:09.120 --> 20:12.230
Truly happy. Of course I'm happy.

20:12.230 --> 20:14.420
I'm just too happy...

20:14.420 --> 20:16.600
So happy to be happy,

20:16.600 --> 20:18.960
to feel happiness...

20:18.960 --> 20:23.540
And that's all the reason you 
need to eat and drink in excess!

20:23.540 --> 20:25.920
The longer you wait for something,

20:25.920 --> 20:28.620
the longer you go hungry...

20:30.100 --> 20:34.170
the more delicious that first bite tastes!

20:35.000 --> 20:36.490
What's this?

20:36.490 --> 20:42.530
My dude, are you someone who 
has something against us?

20:42.530 --> 20:45.630
I mean, you know, we're not very smart,

20:45.630 --> 20:48.930
and we don't have a very good memory.

20:50.640 --> 20:52.730
Look, you little shit.

20:52.730 --> 20:57.080
If you really just ended up here because 
you have no sense of direction,

20:57.080 --> 20:59.170
then spit it out right now.

20:59.170 --> 21:01.570
I can still forgive you. But if—

21:01.570 --> 21:07.620
We are the Sin Archbishop in the 
Witch's Cult representing gluttony,

21:07.620 --> 21:09.950
Roy Alphard.

21:14.010 --> 21:17.250
Gluttony!

21:15.920 --> 21:18.920
<b>Operation: Take Back the Government Office</b>

22:55.790 --> 22:58.560
Where... am I?

23:00.040 --> 23:06.400
Right... I fought with that bandaged 
woman in the town square...

23:06.990 --> 23:08.610
Wait, huh?

23:08.610 --> 23:09.990
I'm naked?!

23:12.470 --> 23:14.700
Ah, it appears you're awake.

23:14.700 --> 23:17.500
I'm so glad you're all right.

23:17.930 --> 23:19.960
I'm relieved from the bottom of my heart.

23:20.740 --> 23:22.920
Um... And you are...

23:22.920 --> 23:27.200
Before I introduce myself, I'd like 
you to answer an important question.

23:27.200 --> 23:30.320
It's vital to our future, you see.

23:30.320 --> 23:31.380
"Our" future?

23:31.830 --> 23:35.080
Emilia, are you a virgin?

23:35.080 --> 23:38.670
That's the one thing that really matters.
